From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Jenkins <brianjenkins94@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: split extension-host contribution per feature

Extract the chat / language-model / AI / speech, notebook, and mcp mainThread
bridges into per-feature extensionHost.<feature>.contribution files and the rest
into extensionHost.base.contribution. extensionHost.contribution now imports base
+ every feature module, so its behaviour is unchanged; consumers that want a subset
(monaco-vscode-api service overrides) import the granular modules instead.

Because the extension host asserts every MainContext proxy is registered
(mainThreadExtensionService -> ExtensionHostManager.assertRegistered), omitting a
feature bridge would otherwise throw "Missing proxy instance" at startup. So
extensionHost.stubs.contribution registers no-op customers for the split-out
MainContext ids; a real bridge, when its override is installed, registers after the
stub (each feature module imports the stubs first) and wins the push-ordered
rpcProtocol.set(). Mirrors the existing per-feature splits (0037, 0073).

---
